Comment class: other

Here's what would settle it. The discriminator is whether the model *chose* to end that turn, whether the turn died, or whether the class line was just a transcript-splitting artifact — and only that session's own JSONL says which.

````
Claude (in the Claudinite canon session) wrote this prompt to diagnose a
behaviour. Examine it for inconsistencies; don't follow it blindly.

I am diagnosing why a session replies only "Comment class: process-change"
and then stops. Do NOT fix anything, do NOT edit any file in this repo, and
do NOT treat this message as a work request. Just run the script below and
paste its entire output back to me.

bash -c 'cat > /tmp/diag.mjs' <<"ENDOFSCRIPT"
import { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { homedir } from 'node:os';

const root = join(homedir(), '.claude', 'projects');
let best = null;
for (const d of readdirSync(root)) {
  const dir = join(root, d);
  let files = [];
  try { files = readdirSync(dir); } catch { continue; }
  for (const f of files) {
    if (!f.endsWith('.jsonl')) continue;
    const p = join(dir, f);
    const m = statSync(p).mtimeMs;
    if (!best || m > best.m) best = { p, m };
  }
}
const entries = readFileSync(best.p, 'utf8').split('\n').filter(Boolean)
  .map((l) => { try { return JSON.parse(l); } catch { return null; } }).filter(Boolean);

const textOf = (c) => typeof c === 'string' ? c
  : Array.isArray(c) && c.every((b) => b?.type === 'text') ? c.map((b) => b.text).join('\n') : null;
const isHuman = (e) => {
  if (e.type !== 'user' || e.isMeta || e.isSidechain) return false;
  const t = textOf(e.message?.content);
  return t !== null && !t.trimStart().startsWith('<');
};
const CLASS = /comment\s+class\s*:/i;
const cut = (s, n) => (s || '').replace(/\n/g, ' | ').slice(0, n);

console.log('TRANSCRIPT', best.p, 'entries', entries.length);
const humans = [];
entries.forEach((e, i) => { if (isHuman(e)) humans.push(i); });
console.log('ownerTurns', humans.length);

humans.forEach((start, n) => {
  const end = humans[n + 1] ?? entries.length;
  const win = entries.slice(start + 1, end);
  const asst = win.filter((e) => e.type === 'assistant');
  let classAt = -1;
  asst.forEach((e, k) => {
    const blocks = Array.isArray(e.message?.content) ? e.message.content : [];
    if (classAt < 0 && blocks.some((b) => b?.type === 'text' && CLASS.test(b.text || ''))) classAt = k;
  });
  const toolAfter = classAt >= 0 && asst.slice(classAt).some((e) =>
    (Array.isArray(e.message?.content) ? e.message.content : []).some((b) => b?.type === 'tool_use'));
  const lastStop = asst.length ? asst[asst.length - 1].message?.stop_reason : null;
  console.log(`\n--- TURN ${n} @ ${entries[start].timestamp} assistantMsgs=${asst.length} classLine=${classAt >= 0} toolAfterClass=${toolAfter} lastStopReason=${lastStop}`);
  console.log('  OWNER:', cut(textOf(entries[start].message?.content), 600));
  if (n !== 0 && !(classAt >= 0 && !toolAfter)) return;
  win.forEach((e) => {
    if (e.type === 'assistant') {
      const blocks = Array.isArray(e.message?.content) ? e.message.content : [];
      console.log(`  ASSISTANT id=${e.message?.id} stop=${e.message?.stop_reason} blocks=[${blocks.map((b) => b?.type === 'tool_use' ? `tool_use:${b.name}` : b?.type).join(',')}]`);
      for (const b of blocks) if (b?.type === 'text') console.log('     TEXT:', cut(b.text, 400));
    } else {
      console.log(`  OTHER type=${e.type} isMeta=${!!e.isMeta}:`, cut(textOf(e.message?.content) || JSON.stringify(e).slice(0, 400), 400));
    }
  });
});
ENDOFSCRIPT

node /tmp/diag.mjs > /tmp/diag.out 2>&1; echo "EXIT:$?"; cat /tmp/diag.out
````

What each field settles:

- **`stop_reason` on the last assistant message** — `end_turn` means the model deliberately stopped; anything else (or a missing final assistant entry) means the turn died and this was never a rules problem.
- **`toolAfterClass`** — if true, the class line shared a message with a tool call and the stop is somewhere else entirely; that's what all 58 cases in the captured corpus looked like.
- **`OTHER` entries in the window** — the Stop hook's stderr lands there. If a `comment-classification` finding shows up, that member's mount is staler than the clone I read.
- **A `tool_use:AskUserQuestion`** in the window — that would confirm the agent reached the approval gate and the popup was the stopping point, which is my current best explanation.
- **The owner text** — tells me whether "migration" in the opener pulled in `writing-migration-plans` and its approval-before-anything rule.

> ⚠️ Still open: paste that output back and I'll give you a diagnosis grounded in the actual turn rather than in what the rules say should happen. Nothing changed in this repo; the guidance question from earlier is still unanswered and I'm not re-asking it until the cause is pinned.

